  "id": "Compound::DB00451 - Gene::353189",
  "verbalization": "Levothyroxine is implicated in the pathogenesis of several disorders, including craniosynostosis, epiphysiolysis, and slipped femoral capital epiphysis, all of which are linked to Liotrix. These conditions are mediated through the binding of Liotrix to Slco4c1, a protein involved in drug transport and metabolism. The shared pathway from Levothyroxine to Liotrix to Slco4c1 suggests a potential mechanism by which Levothyroxine may influence Slco4c1 function, possibly through the indirect effects of Liotrix. The presence of a common ancestor in the Thyroid Agent and Phenylalanine Derivative categories further supports a broader biological context in which Levothyroxine and Liotrix interact. The integrated evidence indicates that Levothyroxine may modulate Slco4c1 through a mechanism involving Liotrix, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated. The observed scores and shared pathways highlight a plausible but not yet fully understood relationship between Levothyroxine and Slco4c1, emphasizing the need for further mechanistic investigation.",
